{"title":"Career Roadmap — CAE Engineer","role":"CAE Engineer","summary":"A CAE (Computer-Aided Engineering) Engineer uses engineering simulation and numerical analysis to predict the behavior, performance, safety, durability, and manufacturability of mechanical products before or alongside physical testing.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Mechanical Engineering (Smart Mechanical / Mechatronics & Automation)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A CAE (Computer-Aided Engineering) Engineer uses engineering simulation and numerical analysis to predict the behavior, performance, safety, durability, and manufacturability of mechanical products before or alongside physical testing."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical domains include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Structural simulation"},{"text":"Finite Element Analysis (FEA)"},{"text":"Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD)"},{"text":"Thermal analysis"},{"text":"Fatigue and durability"},{"text":"NVH"},{"text":"Crash analysis"},{"text":"Multibody dynamics"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"Digital twins"},{"text":"Simulation automation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a Smart Mechanical / Mechatronics & Automation graduate, CAE is a strong career because it combines mechanical engineering with simulation, programming, automation, controls, and data-driven engineering."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"CAD, mechanics, FEM, FEA/CFD and simulation fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialized structural, thermal, CFD, fatigue or dynamics simulation"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Multiphysics, optimization, HPC, digital twins and simulation automation"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"CAE Technical Lead, Simulation Architect, Principal Engineer or Digital Engineering Leader"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 